# suite=stic; columns: <FAULT_ID> <must-fail> <allowed-prefixes> <must-pass>
# STIC named faults (plan 06-06, VID-01, D-05, D-07, D-10, A-06). Each id has one IVS_FAULT_<ID> site, in the owner TU
# named below, and is caught by the test it is named for; the allowed prefixes cover every collateral failure of the suite.
# STIC_FRAME_BY_MODULO (core/src/stic/stic_events.c): the frame index is derived as to_tick / F after the catch-up
# instead of counted by FRAME_END events; a nonzero frame phase makes the two differ.
STIC_FRAME_BY_MODULO stic.events.frame-index-is-state stic.events.frame-index-is-state|stic.events.idempotent stic.events.table-order
# STIC_WINDOW_OFF_BY_ONE (core/src/stic/stic_events.c): an event is applied only when its tick is strictly below the
# stamp, so a gate closes one tick late and an access at the close tick would still be served.
STIC_WINDOW_OFF_BY_ONE stic.events.edges stic.events.|stic.reset.|stic.slice.|stic.window. stic.events.idempotent
# STIC_CATCHUP_LAGS_UNIT (core/src/machine/machine_run.c): the step seam catches the STIC up to the unit START instead of
# the unit end, so the gates and the cursor lag one unit behind machine time.
STIC_CATCHUP_LAGS_UNIT stic.slice.state-equal-at-every-unit-boundary stic.slice.|stic.reset. stic.events.table-order
# STIC_ALIAS_NOT_HOOKED (core/src/machine/machine_bus.c): the STIC_ALIAS_READ hook class is treated as NONE, so a read of a
# mode-select alias address ($4021, $8021, $C021), which the read view decodes to the cartridge, never reaches the STIC:
# no mode switch inside the window and no blocked count outside it.
STIC_ALIAS_NOT_HOOKED stic.alias.read-4021-switches-mode stic.alias. stic.mode.read-selects-cs
# STIC_MODE_SWITCH_OUTSIDE_WINDOW (core/src/machine/machine_bus.c): the access effects (the display-enable strobe, the mode
# selects) are applied even when the gate is closed, so a blocked access still changes the latch or the mode.
STIC_MODE_SWITCH_OUTSIDE_WINDOW stic.mode.read-outside-window-no-effect stic.mode.|stic.alias.|stic.enable.|stic.window.|stic.blocked. stic.events.table-order
